confirmed.fix:
Two corrections to the seat's CSS. First, nowrap must come with min-width:0 or the flex row cannot shrink: `.xaxis span { min-width: 0; white-space: nowrap; }`. Second, thin only in the two bands that actually wrap, keep three anchors not two, and remove the boxes rather than fade them so no min-width is reserved:

@media (max-width: 1140px) and (min-width: 901px), (max-width: 792px) {
  .xaxis span:not(:only-child) { display: none; }
  .xaxis span:not(:only-child):first-child,
  .xaxis span:not(:only-child):nth-child(7),
  .xaxis span:not(:only-child):last-child { display: block; flex: 0 0 auto; }
}

.xaxis already carries justify-content:space-between, so the three survivors land flush-left, centred and flush-right with no text-align overrides — which is what keeps them inside the card. :not(:only-child) leaves the first-run single-tick axis alone. Measured with this applied over states full/partial/quiet/first-run at 1440/1141/1140/1000/901/900/793/792/768/700/560/480/390: axis height is 14.8px (one line) at every width, no tick crosses the card edge, no document horizontal overflow, all five labels retained from 1141 up and from 900 to 793, three from 1140 to 901 and from 792 down. Twelve columns stay twelve throughout; only the labelling thins, which is the seat's own stated intent.

